# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Coding and Workflow Rules Log

This log turns repeated manual corrections and explicit operator workflow
choices into durable, reviewable rules. It is evidence, not telemetry or
automatic write authorization.

## Promotion threshold

Present a candidate when substantially the same manual edit, review correction,
or explicit operator choice:

- appears in at least three locations in the inspected scope; or
- recurs across separate approved tasks, reviews, or regressions.

Do not infer recurrence or preference from silence. Use only current
conversation evidence, approved task records, review results, repository
history, tests, or owner-provided examples. Do not store prompt text, source
content, credentials, personal data, or unrelated behavior metadata.

## Candidate record

For each candidate, record:

| Field | Required content |
| --- | --- |
| ID | Stable `RULE-CANDIDATE-NNN` identifier |
| Status | observed / proposed / approved / enforced / rejected / superseded |
| Evidence | Exact files, reviews, tasks, or test failures showing recurrence |
| Kind | coding / verification-route / approval-scope / output-format / other |
| Scope | Applicable languages, modules, generated/manual code, and exclusions |
| Problem | Why the repeated form harms readability, correctness, or maintenance |
| Replacement | The preferred code shape or rule, with a concise example |
| Conflicts | Existing rules, tools, contracts, or compatibility constraints |
| Enforcement | Prose, formatter, linter, static check, template, generator, or test |
| Migration | Future-only, touched-code, or separately approved historical migration |
| Decision | Approver, approval reference, date, and reason |
| Reconsideration | Condition or date before a rejected candidate may be raised again |

